Z||000007||WKDFIRO||07-10-2000||12:55 PM||||Unless the car has been sitting for a VERY long time I think you should not worry about the fuel filters and concentrate on things that you can get to namely the coilpacs.<P>A way of finding out if you have a cylinder missing is to pull a plug while the engine is running, make sure to keep the plug wire close to the block so it will arc to the block but not you. This will give you an idea of which cyclinder is not firing. If it gets worse then you know that plug is firing. If it doesn't then then you know you found one. If its a coilpac then you would be missing 2 cylinders. Don't do this for too long, its not good for the coilpacs but it would be enough to give you the info. <P>If you have spark, then next is compression testing.<P>Good luck!||||reg||1
