Z||000009||TheFiero64||07-10-2000||05:10 PM||||When I had my 88 Dis engine in my fiero. I had a big problem. (I fixed it.) It would run very bad. It would sound like it was out of time and it misfired and back fired when you hit the gas. I thought it was the module,and the coil pacs. Then I talk to an expert in dis ignition. <B>He said that dis cars need high performance low Ohm plug wires.</B> I got accels with only 500 ohms resistance and it ran like gold. It was the best running 4 I have ever driven!<P>Here is the link for those wires <A HREF="http://www.jegs.com/cgi-bin/ncommerce3/ProductDisplay?prrfnbr=26294&prmenbr=76&path=76%202379%202412%202710" TARGET=_blank>http://www.jegs.com/cgi-bin/ncommerce3/ProductDisplay?prrfnbr=26294&prmenbr=76&path=76%202379%202412%202710</A> <P>------------------<BR>Joshua Bumpus<BR>New Bedford, MA<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fi.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||terryk||07-10-2000||06:59 PM||||DIS's have another notorious problem.<P>If you carbon track a plug, the plug and wire must be replaced. If you carbon track a coil pack, the coil pack and wires must be replaced. <P>The tracking looks like black spiderwebs on the coil or porcelin of the plug.<P>The carbon tracking is usually caused by a bad plug or wire.<P>Trust me, I've benn through this with DIS. When it works, it's great.||||reg||1
